refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
arrayfalsesnmp2_real_walk stringhostname stringcommunity arraystringobject_id inttimeout-1 intretries-1
The snmp2_real_walk function is used to traverse over a number of SNMP objects starting from object_id and return not only their values but also their object ids.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns an associative array of the SNMP object ids and their values on success or &false; on error. In case of an error, an E_WARNING message is shown.
The keys are the object ids, formatted according to snmp_set_oid_output_format. &false; is returned, with an E_WARNING, if the subtree does not exist or is empty, for example "No Such Object" or "No more variables left in this MIB View". It is also returned on an error or a timeout during the walk, in which case the entries already received are discarded.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a ValueError if hostname contains a null byte,
 is 128 bytes long or longer, or has a port outside the range 0 to 65535,
 if community is empty or contains a null byte,
 if timeout is lower than -1,
 if retries is lower than -1 or too large,
 or if object_id is an empty array.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.5.0

     Now throws a ValueError when the hostname
     length is equal to or greater than 128 bytes, when the port is
     negative or greater than 65535, or when the timeout or retries values
     are lower than -1 or too large.
